-</style><p node="[object Object]" class="" data-ag-id="ag-n-112">The risk of overriding the strict isolation protocol and using the default <code node="[object Object]" class="whitespace-pre-wrap" data-ag-id="ag-n-113" style="word-break: break-word;">inherit</code> workspace revolves entirely around <strong data-ag-id="ag-n-114">State Contamination</strong> and <strong data-ag-id="ag-n-115">Failure Recovery</strong>:</p>
-  <ol data-ag-id="ag-n-116">
-  <li node="[object Object]" data-ag-id="ag-n-117"><strong data-ag-id="ag-n-118">Shared Physical Directory (Race Conditions):</strong> The framework's <code node="[object Object]" class="whitespace-pre-wrap" data-ag-id="ag-n-119" style="word-break: break-word;">branch</code> parameter doesn't just create a git branch; it provisions a physically isolated workspace (like a <code node="[object Object]" class="whitespace-pre-wrap" data-ag-id="ag-n-120" style="word-break: break-word;">git worktree</code> or clone). If we use <code node="[object Object]" class="whitespace-pre-wrap" data-ag-id="ag-n-121" style="word-break: break-word;">inherit</code>, the subagent will be executing its Agentic TDD protocol (writing tests, failing them, refactoring code, and running linters) directly in your active <code node="[object Object]" class="whitespace-pre-wrap" data-ag-id="ag-n-122" style="word-break: break-word;">C:\Users\nferr\OneDrive\Documents\Projects\cortex</code> folder. If you try to run or test the app while the subagent is working, your app might crash due to half-written code.</li>
-  <li node="[object Object]" data-ag-id="ag-n-123"><strong data-ag-id="ag-n-124">Destructive Hallucinations &amp; Git Conflicts:</strong> If the subagent goes off the rails and deletes files or hallucinates broken dependencies, it happens directly in your main folder. Furthermore, if it manually runs <code node="[object Object]" class="whitespace-pre-wrap" data-ag-id="ag-n-125" style="word-break: break-word;">git checkout -b</code> in the shared directory, it will instantly change your local Git state, potentially interfering with any uncommitted changes you have lying around.</li>
-  <li node="[object Object]" data-ag-id="ag-n-126"><strong data-ag-id="ag-n-127">Loss of the "Undo" Button:</strong> The primary benefit of the framework-level <code node="[object Object]" class="whitespace-pre-wrap" data-ag-id="ag-n-128" style="word-break: break-word;">branch</code> is that if the subagent fails or deadlocks, I (the Parent Orchestrator) can simply <code node="[object Object]" class="whitespace-pre-wrap" data-ag-id="ag-n-129" style="word-break: break-word;">kill</code> it. The framework immediately vaporizes the sandboxed directory, leaving your main repository 100% pristine. Without it, killing a rogue subagent leaves your main repository in a broken, half-committed state that requires manual git cleanups.</li>
-  </ol>
-  <p node="[object Object]" class="" data-ag-id="ag-n-130">If you are confident that your current <code node="[object Object]" class="whitespace-pre-wrap" data-ag-id="ag-n-131" style="word-break: break-word;">cortex</code> git working tree is clean and you don't mind the subagent working in the live folder, you can authorize me to bypass the rule. Alternatively, setting the active workspace in your Antigravity IDE UI will allow the framework to spin up the protective sandbox automatically!</p></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class="flex flex-col py-1 gap-1.5" data-ag-id="ag-n-132"></div></div><div class="pt-3" data-ag-id="ag-n-133"><div data-ag-id="ag-n-134"><div class="flex flex-col gap-2" data-ag-id="ag-n-135"><div class="flex w-full justify-between items-start gap-1 pl-2 pr-1" data-ag-id="ag-n-136"><div class="text-xs grow opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-60 text-foreground transition-opacity whitespace-nowrap flex items-center h-5" data-ag-id="ag-n-137">9:33 PM</div><div class="flex items-center" data-ag-id="ag-n-138"><button class="inline-flex items-center font-medium transition-colors select-none outline-none cursor-pointer justify-center disabled:opacity-50 bg-transparent text-muted-foreground hover:text-foreground hover:bg-secondary h-6 w-6 shrink-0 flex items-center justify-center rounded-md text-secondary-foreground hover:text-foreground" data-tooltip-id="copy-:r2nd:" aria-label="Copy" data-tooltip-place="top-end" data-ag-id="ag-n-139"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 -960 960 960" fill="currentColor" class="h-4 w-4" data-ag-id="ag-n-140"><path d="M362.31-260Q332-260 311-281t-21-51.31V-787.69Q290-818 311-839t51.31-21H697.69Q728-860 749-839t21,51.31v455.38Q770-302 749-281t-51.31,21H362.31Zm0-60H697.69q4.62,0 8.46-3.85t3.85-8.46V-787.69q0-4.62-3.85-8.46T697.69-800H362.31q-4.62,0-8.46,3.85T350-787.69v455.38q0,4.62 3.85,8.46t8.46,3.85Zm-140,200Q192-120 171-141t-21-51.31V-707.69h60v515.38q0,4.62 3.85,8.46t8.46,3.85